### Compass lookup administration — employee types and invoice frequency types
###
### Every route requires the Compass Super Admin policy. A "Compass Admin" principal is refused with
### 403 on ALL of these, reads included (FR-009) — that role is read-only in Compass however
### administrative the name sounds (AC-44).
###
### Locally, `make dev-all` runs DevBypass, so requests are already authenticated. Confirm you actually
### hold the role before blaming a 403:
###   curl -s http://localhost:5009/api/me | jq '.privileges'
### If "Compass Super Admin" is missing, fix the bypass principal's groups. Do NOT relax a policy to
### make a request work.
###
### There is deliberately NO DELETE. A lookup is retired by PUTting isActive false, which leaves every
### record already classified by it untouched (FR-007). These writes are also deliberately NOT audited
### (FR-008, AC-NFR-3) — the one Compass configuration surface outside the audit trail.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5009

### Employee types — all of them (what the admin screen requests)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types
Accept: application/json

### Employee types — active only (what the EDJEr configuration form requests, AC-25)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types?activeOnly=true
Accept: application/json

### Add an employee type — created ACTIVE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Contract"
}

### Add a duplicate — expect 409 (FR-004). Case and surrounding whitespace do not make it distinct.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "  contract  "
}

### Add a blank name — expect 400, not 409. Malformed is not the same as colliding.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "   "
}

### Rename an employee type (replace 1 with a real id)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Contractor",
  "isActive": true
}

### Retire an employee type — the same route, isActive false. Records already using it are unchanged.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Contractor",
  "isActive": false
}

### Unknown id — expect 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types/424242
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Nowhere",
  "isActive": true
}

### No DELETE exists — expect 405
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/employee-types/1

### Invoice frequency types — all of them
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/invoice-frequency-types
Accept: application/json

### Invoice frequency types — active only (the client form's invoicing default, AC-26)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/invoice-frequency-types?activeOnly=true
Accept: application/json

### Add an invoice frequency type. The two lookups are independent name spaces — a name already used
### as an employee type is accepted here (FR-006).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/invoice-frequency-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Fortnightly"
}

### Rename / retire an invoice frequency type (replace 1 with a real id)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/compass/v1/admin/invoice-frequency-types/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeName": "Fortnightly",
  "isActive": false
}
